We choose index i and final value v for it. Final array: nums[i] = v, and for j ≠ i, nums[j] stays or changes. Constraint: for all j ≠ i, gcd(v, final[j]) = 1. Min cost: for j ≠ i, if gcd(v, nums[j]) == 1, keep (cost 0), else change to 1 (cost 1). Plus cost for i: 0 if nums[i] == v else 1 (change to v, requires v ≤ maxVal).

Total min cost for (i, v) [v ≤ maxVal or v == nums[i]]:
C(i,v) = [nums[i] != v] + sum_{j≠i} [gcd(v, nums[j]) != 1]

Define bad(v) = sum_j [gcd(v, nums[j]) != 1] (over all j).
sum_{j≠i} = bad(v) - [gcd(v, nums[i]) != 1].

C(i,v) = [nums[i] != v] + bad(v) - [gcd(v, nums[i]) != 1].

Score(i,v) = v - C(i,v) = v - bad(v) - [nums[i] != v] + [gcd(v, nums[i]) != 1].

Maximize over i: max of (- [nums[i] != v] + [gcd(v, nums[i]) != 1]).

- If some i has nums[i] == v: term = -0 + [gcd(v,v) != 1] = [v != 1] = (1 if v>1 else 0).
- Else if some i has gcd(v, nums[i]) != 1 (i.e., bad(v) > 0): term = -1 + 1 = 0.
- Else: term = -1 + 0 = -1.

So maxScore(v):
- cnt[v] > 0: v - bad(v) + (1 if v > 1 else 0)
- cnt[v] == 0 and bad(v) > 0: v - bad(v)
- cnt[v] == 0 and bad(v) == 0: v - 1

For v ≤ maxVal, all three cases possible. For v > maxVal, only allowed if cnt[v] > 0 (must select unchanged element with that value), giving v - bad(v) + 1 (v > 1 since v > maxVal ≥ 1).

