Now, one more subtle point: for v ≤ maxVal with cnt[v] > 0, we select i with nums[i] = v, no change to i. But what if bad(v) counts i itself (gcd(v,v) = v > 1, counted in bad(v))? Yes, bad(v) includes i. sum_{j≠i} = bad(v) - 1. C = 0 + bad(v) - 1. Score = v - bad(v) + 1. Correct.

For v = 1 with cnt[1] > 0: bad(1) = 0 (gcd(1, anything) = 1). C = 0 + 0 - 0 = 0. Score = 1. Formula: v - bad + 0 = 1. Correct.

