```python
def brute(nums, maxVal):
    from math import gcd
    n = len(nums)
    best = -10**18
    for i in range(n):
        candidates = set(range(1, maxVal+1)) | {nums[i]}
        for v in candidates:
            if v > maxVal and v != nums[i]:
                continue
            cost = 0
            if nums[i] != v:
                cost += 1
            ok = True
            for j in range(n):
                if j == i: continue
                if gcd(v, nums[j]) != 1:
                    cost += 1  # change to 1
            best = max(best, v - cost)
    return best
```

This is O(n * (maxVal) * n) which for small inputs is fine. I'll compare on random small tests.

